11domain features (using FFT or spectral analysis).  \n- Train separate RUL models (e.g., LSTM or transformer) on time\u2011only features and on the combined feature set.  \n- Predict the remaining life for all test bearings.  \n- Compute MAE/RMSE for each model and directly compare the results, giving you the concrete numbers you need.\n\nWithout access to the MFPT data in a supported format, the requested prediction and comparison cannot be performed here. If you can upload the dataset or convert it to a compatible format, please let me know and I\u2019ll proceed with the full analysis.", "payload": null, "status_code": null, "execution_time_ms": null, "source": "unavailable"}], "provenance": {"logprobs": "provider", "confidence": "unavailable", "status_code": "unavailable"}}
{"step_index": 2, "thought": "Question: The MFPT dataset was captured at a very high sampling rate (97.656KHz), so there is probably useful information in the frequency domain. Can you predict remaining life for all test bearings using both time and frequency domain features, verify the predictions, and tell me if adding frequency analysis improves accuracy compared to just using time\u2011domain data? I need concrete numbers to justify the extra processing.\n\nThought: The available tools can load and model only the CMAPSS turbofan\u2011engine datasets and the CWRU bearing dataset. There is no tool for loading the MFPT bearing dataset, nor for extracting frequency\u2011domain features from it. Consequently I cannot train RUL models on that data, generate predictions, or compute MAE/RMSE to compare time\u2011only versus time\u2011plus\u2011frequency models.", "action": "Question: The MFPT dataset was captured at a very high sampling rate (97.656KHz), so there is probably useful information in the frequency domain. Can you predict remaining life for all test bearings using both time and frequency domain features, verify the predictions, and tell me if adding frequency analysis improves accuracy compared to just using time\u2011domain data? I need concrete numbers to justify the extra processing.\n\nThought: The available tools can load and model only the CMAPSS turbofan\u2011engine datasets and the CWRU bearing dataset. There is no tool for loading the MFPT bearing dataset, nor for extracting frequency\u2011domain features from it. Consequently I cannot train RUL models on that data, generate predictions, or compute MAE/RMSE to compare time\u2011only versus time\u2011plus\u2011frequency models.\n\nFinal Answer: I\u2019m unable to perform the requested analysis on the MFPT bearing dataset with the current toolset. The environment only supports loading and modeling the CMAPSS and CWRU datasets; it does not include a loader or feature\u2011extraction routine for the hig